@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 -->
+# ProductProgram representation and constructor phase
+
+This implementation layer is based on the corrected 288-file source manifest
+with SHA-256 `ede5cfafab73e79657c4680398156b84cc4ce62f6fd4fb50a4ef4dba2e16207b`.
+It implements part of the common ProductProgram design. It does not qualify the
+whole geometry platform or replace the processing session's attempt authority.
+
+`geometry/program/traversal.rs` owns the admitted product, ordered selected
+representations, current whole item list, representation/item cursor and
+annotation policy. Both ordinary merged and styled consumers use it through the
+unchanged router entrypoints. Alignment and material layers retain their prior
+early entry points. No source descendants are lowered before their item runs.
+The original duplicated product representation loops are removed.
+
+`program/source.rs` admits the actual whole item list and owns its ordered
+occurrences. Product, merged mapped source, styled mapped source and type-map
+consumers use the same adapter. Required product and required map errors retain
+their distinct messages; styled mapped sources retain optional missing Items.
+Claims stay at the caller's historical point: after bulk Items for merged maps,
+before optional Items for styled maps, and after Items for type maps. This shared
+item-list control does not migrate the mapping enter/exit state machines.
+
+`program/resources.rs` owns the merged product's ordinary, RTC and distant-frame
+accumulators, bounds and single-instance eligibility. Its numerical merge and
+finish operations receive meshes and an explicit reached instancing policy;
+they cannot decode source. They preserve the original merge order and complete
+Mesh metadata. Placement and source hygiene remain at their existing sites.
+
+The shared `program::OwnedConstructor` encapsulates the actual nineteen built-in
+constructor payloads, including valid empty swept constructors. The selected
+`GeometryProcessor` instance admits these through `lower_owned`; family metadata
+does not select a replacement processor. `program/execute.rs` evaluates these
+owned payloads without a decoder or router. The optional ConstructionBatch uses
+the same payload, while retaining its separate eager graph and operand policy.
+Boolean operand empty flags and recorders remain in their current continuations.
+
+Default custom registrations decline owned lowering and retain their mutable
+process/RTC callbacks under the existing synchronous execution owner. Built-in
+raw-coordinate admission receives the same reached file-unit RTC offset; numeric
+validation, scale, bounds publication, curve/face drains and cache publication
+remain at their historical sites. Alignment's selected constructor uses the same
+admission hook. A lower failure does not try another implementation.
+
+This layer remains synchronous. ProductProgram is crate-private and does not
+expose transferable requests or replies. It holds no borrowed decoder, budget,
+transaction, unsupported-counting or triangle-order guard. Source bytes/index
+coherence is not authenticated by these lifecycle or ownership types.
+
+Remaining control includes mapping source/transform/cache/occurrence frames,
+boolean/CSG child frames, texture fallback and UV construction, type-map origin
+and finish, material-layer eligibility/slice, placement, opening classification,
+source capture and numeric application. Those branches keep their existing
+canonical implementation. In particular, `session_work.rs` still has coarse
+outer work requests. There is no second loader or alternate production engine.
+Exact Rust arithmetic remains permanent and default.
+
+Resource reservations, terminal cancellation/refusal, effect receipts, complete
+source authentication, finer request identities and cross-platform/full-scene
+qualification remain open. Existing depth/path and exact-kernel budgets retain
+their previous scope; no new global visited suppression or arbitrary cap is
+introduced. No performance or memory improvement is claimed by this extraction.
